# UNVERIFIED Merlin-shaped parameterization: pending the discovery
# evidence from the parallel Merlin capture worker, no claim is made
# that this matches the PSI Merlin A100 partition's real Slingshot
# wiring.
#
# What discovery from five NCCL-over-sockets nodes can actually
# determine: the per-NIC-port rate (200 Gbit/s), the number of ports
# per node (4), and coarse effective latency between node pairs.  It
# cannot determine the site-wide dragonfly shape, so this instance is
# the smallest fabric consistent with those observables: all twenty
# 200G NIC ports of the five A100 nodes attached to one Rosetta-class
# switch (a 64-port Rosetta comfortably hosts 20 endpoint ports), that
# is p = 20, a = 1, h = 0, g = 1.  Every endpoint pair crosses exactly
# one switch and routing degenerates to delivery; the progressive
# adaptive machinery is exercised only by multi-group instances.
#
# Endpoint numbering: host = node * 4 + port for node in 0..4 and
# port in 0..3.
#
# The latency figures below are placeholders at the fixture defaults
# and are exactly the values the calibration wave must replace from
# the capture-derived evidence.  Status: hosted, calibration pending.
topology dragonfly
hosts_per_router 20
routers_per_group 1
global_links_per_router 0
groups 1
host_link_gbps 200
host_link_latency_ps 300000
switch_pipeline_ps 350000
rosetta_buffer_bytes 4194304
max_wire_packet_bytes 4160
routing_seed 383530136519245852
